  "question": {
    "text": "If <math><mi>A</mi></math>, <math><mi>B</mi></math> are two non-singular matrices of order <math><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math>&nbsp;is an identity matrix of order&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> such that <math><mi>A</mi><msup><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ι</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, then <math><msup><mrow><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is equal to (where&nbsp;<math><msup><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced></math> denote transpose and adjoint matrices of the matrix <math><mi>A</mi></math> respectively)",
